Hmm, for state "incomplete" or "stopped-early", playable true → opens file. OK.

Download link only when `playback.status === "ready"` — uses `playback` (not `shown`), fine.

Delete dialog shown when `row.state !== "recording"`.

`onConfirm`: calls remover; on success `setDeleted(true); setConfirmOpen(false); onDeleted(row);`. `returnFocus={!deleted}` — dialog closes via controlled `open` state; finalFocus false since screen moves focus itself. OK.

But — one issue: `onDeleted` triggers navigation to /recordings list; the component unmounts; `setDeleted`/`setConfirmOpen` called before navigate — fine.

Potential bug: When delete succeeds but `onDeleted` navigates via `void navigate({ to: "/recordings", replace: true })`. With `replace: true`, the hash changes to empty. The hash-change effect fires: current.kind === "list", returnItem set → focusItem or h1. Good.

But wait — in `RecordingDetailView`, after `onDeleted`, `detailRow` becomes null quickly; the screen may render NotFoundView briefly before navigation completes? `navigate` is async; during that render, list no longer contains row → NotFoundView flashes. Minor.

21. **recording-items.tsx** -

```js
function usePosterUrl(row: LibraryRow): string | null {
  const playable = row.state !== "recording" && row.state !== "missing";
  const playback = useRecordingPlayback(playable ? row.id : null);
