Space on a button activates the button itself (default behavior); returning null lets default happen. But when target is the scrubber INPUT (range), Space... range inputs don't do much with space; `onScrubber` not checked — Space on scrubber triggers toggle and preventDefault. That's OK.

But wait — `case "k": case "K"` etc. — when focus is on the SELECT, they return early with null for all keys. Good.

