`Stage`: `<video ... onClick={player.toggle} {...player.videoEvents} />` — video element without controls, not focusable (video elements are focusable by default in some browsers... typically not tabbable without controls). Keyboard access via region keys. OK.

`ControlRow` RangeInput: `value={duration === null ? 0 : Math.min(time, duration)}` — when duration null, disabled. OK.

Fullscreen: `player.fullscreenAvailable = document.fullscreenEnabled` — computed at render; in Safari (webkit) fullscreenEnabled exists now. OK.

`RecordingPlayer` renders `<section ref={player.regionRef} aria-label="Recording player" onKeyDown=...>`. Hmm — `regionRef` typed `React.RefObject<HTMLElement | null>` and used as section ref — fine.

24. **use-video-player.ts** -

